.5,32.5 220.0,32.0 220.5,31.5 221.0,31.0 221.5,30.5 222.0,30.0 222.5,29.5 223.0,29.0 223.5,28.5 224.0,28.0 224.5,27.5 225.0,27.0 225.5,26.5 226.0,26.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#bbb\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">f(x) = 2x + 3 and f⁻¹(x) = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">x−3</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span> are mirror images in y = x.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Find the inverse of f(x) = 3x − 6.","steps":["Swap x and y: x = 3y − 6.","Make y the subject: 3y = x + 6.","f⁻¹(x) = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">x+6</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span> = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">3</span></span>x + 2."]},"watch":"f⁻¹(x) is not <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"d\">f(x)</span></span>. The −1 means “inverse”, not “one over”.<br><br><b>Problem-solving lens</b><br>Check an inverse by putting a number through f and then through f⁻¹: you must get the number back.","qs":[{"text":"f(x) = 4x + 1. Find f⁻¹(9).","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"f⁻¹(9)","a":"2","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Solve 4x + 1 = 9.","steps":"1. Rule: f⁻¹ undoes f. If f(a) = b, then f⁻¹(b) = a, and the point (a; b) on f becomes (b; a) on f⁻¹ (a reflection in the line y = x).<br>2. f⁻¹(9) is the x for which f(x) = 9<br>3. 4x + 1 = 9, so 4x = 8<br>4. x = 2, so f⁻¹(9) = 2"},{"text":"f(x) = 5x","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"f⁻¹(x) ="}],"hint":"Swap, divide by 5.","steps":"1. Rule (inverse function): write y = f(x), swap x and y, then make y the subject. The result is f⁻¹(x).<br>2. y = 5x. Swap: x = 5y<br>3. Divide by 5: y = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span><br>4. f⁻¹(x) = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"d\">5</span></span>"},{"text":"f(x) = 2x − 8","vis":"","self":1,"parts":[{"label":"f⁻¹(x) ="}],"hint":"Swap, add 8, divide by 2.","steps":"1. Rule (inverse function): write y = f(x), swap x and y, then make y the subject. The result is f⁻¹(x).<br>2. y = 2x − 8. Swap: x = 2y − 8<br>3. x + 8 = 2y<br>4. f⁻¹(x) = <span class=\"fr\"><span class=\"n\">x + 8</span><span class=\"d\">2</span></span>"}]}